      "role": "user",
      "content": "The results are in. Overall, the network traffic looks stable and the endpoint protection is holding up well. But I noticed a note in the logs about some legacy authentication protocols being flagged for something. I don't want to freak the board out with technical minutiae if it's just a routine patch, but if it's a fundamental flaw, I need to know. Based on what your system is seeing in the audit, is our core auth architecture solid, or are we looking at a massive rebuild?",
